  "scope": "The whole area formula of Federer 3.2.20, pp. 256--257: for an H^m measurable finite-mass (H^m,m) rectifiable W and a Lipschitz partial map with exactly domain W, m at most the target dimension, every extended-real target weight has identical source and target integral value graphs. Includes positive and negative infinite values and undefined signed differences. The intrinsic approximate Jacobian has exactly the actual approximate-differentiability domain. Its partial exterior-word least bound agrees with the usual top exterior operator norm on regular tangent m-planes, including degree zero. The exceptional nonlinear-cone interpretation is explicit.",
