  "proof_route": "Prove top-exterior volume scaling and the exact intrinsic chart Jacobian product from the partial chain rule of 3.2.19. Establish local finite multiplicity on compact source charts via 3.2.3 and the Lipschitz Jacobian bound. Extend finite-real transformation 3.2.5(2) to arbitrary extended-real weights by weighted truncations and monotone convergence. Prove both local compact-chart area transformations. Disjoint source cutoffs yield global density measurability; counting-measure additivity yields actual fibre-count sums off the null image of the remainder. Prove measurable and almost-everywhere finite global multiplicity independently from 2.10.11 and a Borel sandwich. Use dominated measurable subproducts and finite multiplicity representatives to transport countable nonnegative sums in both directions, then reconstruct exact signed integral graphs. Preserve the original partial source map and Jacobian domain through opaque extension laws.",
